<title>USA: Sinclair explores acquisitions.</title>
<headline>Sinclair explores acquisitions.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sinclair Broadcast Group Inc said on Tuesday that it is exploring acquisitions of television and radio stations, including a recent bid of more than $500 million for certain broadcasting stations.</p>
<p>Sinclair has engaged in negotiations regarding this bid and other potential deals, but it has not yet reached any definitive agreements or letters of intent, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement was issued in response to recent activity of the company's stock. Sinclair shares fell 5/8 to 30-1/4 on 218,400 shares.  </p>
<p>Sinclair said it will not make further comment about any potential acquisitions until an agreement is reached, but it would not make assurances that the deals could be completed.</p>
<p>Completion of the deals could result in &quot;substantial additional indebtedness,&quot; the company said.</p>
</text>
